WEBVTT

00:05.797 --> 00:07.757
[whistling]

00:11.928 --> 00:13.972
ZOMBIE APOCALYPSE IN KOREA

00:14.764 --> 00:15.849
Hello, everyone!

00:15.932 --> 00:19.102
I'm Orangibberish, and I always get
to the truth behind the rumors.

00:19.185 --> 00:22.605
Okay, today, I'll be uncovering the truth
behind the Hyosan zombies rumor.

00:22.689 --> 00:24.899
I'm on my way to see
if it's really turned into Zombieland

00:24.983 --> 00:27.193
like they've been saying online
and on social media.

00:27.277 --> 00:28.611
You know what I'm talking about.

00:28.695 --> 00:30.029
FINALLY
HE'S REALLY GOING

00:30.113 --> 00:32.198
Whoa. It's already pretty crazy.

00:32.282 --> 00:33.283
Look out there.

00:33.825 --> 00:36.578
[car horns honking]

00:36.661 --> 00:37.871
[sighs]

00:37.954 --> 00:39.748
[grunting]

00:40.540 --> 00:41.791
[Orangibberish] Do you see that?

00:41.875 --> 00:45.253
It's bumper to bumper
with cars trying to get into Hyosan.

00:45.336 --> 00:46.629
There are so many cars.

00:46.713 --> 00:47.756
Hold on.

00:47.839 --> 00:49.966
I'm gonna have to get out
and hike my way in.

00:50.884 --> 00:53.470
[Orangibberish] I came up the mountain
to avoid the traffic jam.

00:54.012 --> 00:55.096
See that there?

00:55.847 --> 00:57.891
That is Hyosan all the way
down there in the distance.

00:57.974 --> 00:59.976
Okay. I'll…
[grunts]

01:00.060 --> 01:02.479
…show you the gear…
[breathes deeply]

01:02.562 --> 01:04.105
…that I've brought for this mission.

01:04.189 --> 01:06.566
First. A helmet.

01:07.358 --> 01:09.402
A hockey mask. A pair of knee pads.

01:09.486 --> 01:11.446
Shin guards. Very important.

01:11.529 --> 01:13.782
This is emergency food.

01:13.865 --> 01:15.992
First aid kit. And water.

01:16.076 --> 01:18.286
And the most important of all, an axe.

01:18.369 --> 01:20.789
If something grabs me,
slice them up like roast beef.

01:20.872 --> 01:21.831
Like that.

01:21.915 --> 01:24.793
Please hit like and subscribe, okay?

01:24.876 --> 01:26.920
MY MOM TOLD ME TO STAY HOME
LOOK AT YOU ALL GEARED UP

01:27.003 --> 01:27.962
[whispers]
Hold on.

01:28.463 --> 01:29.422
RUN! RUN FASTER!

01:29.506 --> 01:31.549
-Shit!
-[zombies growling]

01:31.633 --> 01:34.052
I'm so screwed! Damn these crazy assholes!

01:34.135 --> 01:35.428
THIS IS SCRIPTED, ISN'T IT?

01:35.512 --> 01:36.554
[panting]

01:36.638 --> 01:38.515
IT SHOULD BE OVER SOON
THIS FOOTAGE WILL HELP US

01:38.598 --> 01:39.724
[zombies snarling]

01:39.808 --> 01:42.268
LOOK AT THAT ACTING
THIS IS FUN

01:42.352 --> 01:44.187
Are they gone?
[panting]

01:44.270 --> 01:45.647
TAKE OUT YOUR AXE!

01:45.730 --> 01:48.817
Shit. They're so aggressive.

01:48.900 --> 01:50.777
SHOW US THE STREET
COME BACK

01:52.111 --> 01:54.531
[snarling]

01:56.157 --> 01:58.076
I DON'T THINK I CAN SLEEP TONIGHT
GOODBYE

01:58.159 --> 02:01.538
Did you see that shit?
Yes, I'm talking to you, assholes!

02:01.621 --> 02:04.999
[breathing shakily]

02:05.083 --> 02:06.960
IT'S SCARY
WHERE ARE THE REAL ZOMBIES?

02:07.710 --> 02:11.005
[snarling]

02:11.089 --> 02:12.966
YOU SHOULD'VE TAKEN A GUN
ZOMBIE!

02:13.049 --> 02:14.926
[snarling continues]

02:24.811 --> 02:28.022
[helicopter whirring]

02:34.404 --> 02:36.948
[wind gusting]

02:38.032 --> 02:42.036
[zombies growling]

02:49.711 --> 02:50.795
[groans]

02:53.089 --> 02:55.300
[zombies growling]

03:01.598 --> 03:03.433
[faint snarling]

03:12.358 --> 03:13.359
Are you okay?

03:15.987 --> 03:17.030
Your hand.

03:23.077 --> 03:24.120
You're not okay.

03:25.455 --> 03:27.874
[panting]

03:33.338 --> 03:34.547
[whispers]
Gyeong-su?

03:34.631 --> 03:36.215
Gyeong-su. It's you, isn't it?

03:38.217 --> 03:40.929
-It's me. Cheong-san's mom.
-[snarls]

03:41.012 --> 03:43.056
Gyeong-su. Where's Cheong-san?

03:44.724 --> 03:46.559
[On-jo] I'm sorry to say this…

03:50.647 --> 03:51.940
but you have to be strong.

03:52.815 --> 03:53.775
Don't comfort me.

03:55.777 --> 03:57.195
You can't do things like that.

03:57.946 --> 04:00.323
Yes, I can.

04:04.452 --> 04:05.662
Still, don't do it.

04:10.291 --> 04:11.668
I didn't know…

04:15.213 --> 04:17.131
I-sak was such a precious friend.

04:20.385 --> 04:22.095
When I though she was gone…

04:23.805 --> 04:25.348
it felt like I'd lost the whole world.

04:25.431 --> 04:27.433
[somber music]

04:31.271 --> 04:32.105
Gyeong-su…

04:35.108 --> 04:37.110
must be out there somewhere.

04:37.694 --> 04:38.653
Mm-hm.

04:42.073 --> 04:43.741
-[growls]
-[screams]

04:43.825 --> 04:45.827
Oh! Gyeong-su!

04:46.703 --> 04:49.122
Gyeong-su. I'm Cheong-san's mom.

04:49.205 --> 04:52.041
[snarling]

04:54.127 --> 04:57.088
[whimpering]

04:58.381 --> 05:00.133
Gyeong-su. Aah!

05:01.384 --> 05:03.720
[screaming]

05:04.762 --> 05:06.931
-[flesh squelching]
-Cheong-san…

05:08.725 --> 05:11.352
[helicopter whirring]

05:28.119 --> 05:29.954
I wonder if things are okay outside.

05:31.289 --> 05:33.875
Your dad's a firefighter,
so I'm sure he's fine.

05:35.418 --> 05:37.754
And I'm guessing my mom and dad
are at the restaurant.

05:39.881 --> 05:41.841
That's the most important thing to my mom.

05:43.176 --> 05:45.803
She's probably out there selling chickens
to the zombies right now.

05:49.015 --> 05:50.933
I really wish I could have
some of her chicken.

05:52.101 --> 05:55.104
-You said it was salty.
-But it still tasted good.

05:59.525 --> 06:00.401
Let's eat it…

06:02.612 --> 06:04.614
once it's all over and we get out of here.

06:08.409 --> 06:10.411
[tense music]

06:17.877 --> 06:19.879
[helicopter whirring]

06:24.175 --> 06:26.177
[theme music]

06:26.969 --> 06:30.973
[squelching]

06:41.192 --> 06:44.195
[all snarling]

06:49.283 --> 06:51.035
I didn't hear anything at all.

06:53.746 --> 06:55.456
I just couldn't hear anything.

06:56.165 --> 06:58.584
-Like what?
-I mean, after Na-yeon went out…

06:58.668 --> 07:00.586
[sobbing]

07:03.214 --> 07:05.049
…and then Miss Park went after her.

07:07.218 --> 07:08.469
Miss Park! Miss Park!

07:09.595 --> 07:11.180
I didn't hear anything after that.

07:11.764 --> 07:13.224
You mean, screaming?

07:14.600 --> 07:15.601
Yeah.

07:18.688 --> 07:19.772
Maybe they didn't die, then.

07:21.274 --> 07:23.901
They wouldn't have been quiet
if zombies were biting them.

07:25.194 --> 07:26.529
They must be alive.

07:26.612 --> 07:27.822
[sighs]

07:34.370 --> 07:35.788
Why won't you respond?

07:36.456 --> 07:39.667
No one answers me.
I'm always talking to myself.

07:40.376 --> 07:42.044
-I think you're right.
-Forget it.

07:42.712 --> 07:44.422
I didn't hear anything, either.

07:44.505 --> 07:45.715
Me neither.

07:46.632 --> 07:50.928
I was scared because I didn't know
how I'd feel if I heard them screaming,

07:51.554 --> 07:52.805
but I didn't hear anything.

07:53.556 --> 07:55.766
Come to think of it, neither did I.

07:56.851 --> 07:59.270
Then I'm right. They're alive, right?

08:01.397 --> 08:02.398
Should she be alive?

08:03.941 --> 08:04.942
What do you mean?

08:08.529 --> 08:09.530
She's a murderer.

08:10.323 --> 08:13.034
[Ji-min] She killed Gyeong-su
and walked out of here on her own.

08:13.618 --> 08:16.579
Is it even right for her to be alive?
Aren't you all being fake?

08:16.662 --> 08:17.747
What about Miss Park?

08:18.956 --> 08:20.374
Should she have died too?

08:20.458 --> 08:21.709
[Ji-min] Is that our fault?

08:21.792 --> 08:24.504
Either way, we're responsible
for what happened.

08:24.587 --> 08:25.421
Why is that?

08:26.839 --> 08:27.882
What did we do wrong?

08:28.841 --> 08:31.052
Na-yeon killed someone,
then played the victim,

08:31.135 --> 08:32.553
and chose to leave on her own…

08:34.931 --> 08:36.807
because we didn't listen to her.

08:38.017 --> 08:40.228
If no one's on your side,
is it okay to kill?

08:42.021 --> 08:44.273
[Ji-min] Miss Park acted
like we were wrong.

08:46.442 --> 08:48.611
We didn't tell Na-yeon to go out there.

08:50.905 --> 08:53.074
We didn't tell Miss Park
to go out there, either.

08:55.826 --> 08:57.078
Why should we feel bad?

09:01.123 --> 09:03.459
-What the hell did we do wrong?
-[sighs]

09:03.543 --> 09:05.545
[gloomy music]

09:23.813 --> 09:24.647
Hey.

09:26.399 --> 09:28.192
I feel weird saying this, but--

09:28.276 --> 09:30.194
-Don't say it.
-[groans]

09:34.407 --> 09:36.617
Does anyone else have to go
to the bathroom by any chance?

09:45.459 --> 09:46.752
Am I the only one?

09:49.130 --> 09:50.131
I do.

09:51.966 --> 09:53.509
We have to go, too, actually.

09:54.135 --> 09:55.136
But we can't go out.

10:03.561 --> 10:04.770
[sighs]

10:11.777 --> 10:13.029
[Eun-ji] See?

10:14.655 --> 10:16.198
I told you no one would come.

10:19.160 --> 10:20.911
No one cares about this school.

10:21.746 --> 10:23.748
If they did,
they would've saved us by now.

10:25.041 --> 10:26.709
So we wouldn't have been
attacked like that.

10:36.594 --> 10:37.762
[Cheol-su sighs]

10:51.817 --> 10:53.861
Now, I really wish the school
would burn down.

10:56.072 --> 10:57.823
Till nothing's left.

10:58.616 --> 10:59.825
They'll save us.

11:05.748 --> 11:06.999
They just have to.

11:10.544 --> 11:12.755
[laughing]

11:12.838 --> 11:14.006
[Cheol-su] Otherwise…

11:16.384 --> 11:17.343
I don't know.

11:20.137 --> 11:21.806
I hope there really is a fire…

11:25.184 --> 11:26.727
that kills everyone.

11:28.854 --> 11:29.730
[Eun-ji] Right?

11:32.525 --> 11:33.859
You want to die too?

11:39.407 --> 11:40.491
[Cheol-su exhales sharply]

11:41.200 --> 11:42.201
No.

11:43.285 --> 11:44.620
I know you wanna live.

11:48.916 --> 11:50.418
You wanna live so badly…

11:53.337 --> 11:54.547
that you want to die.

11:58.342 --> 12:01.429
Why are you blaming me for this?
Su-hyeok brought it up.

12:02.513 --> 12:03.639
Pooping's not a crime.

12:05.683 --> 12:07.101
It's not a crime, but…

12:07.184 --> 12:09.395
But what? Don't you need to go?

12:10.187 --> 12:11.647
Yes, I do.

12:12.231 --> 12:15.359
-Not poop, but, you know…
-What about you?

12:18.446 --> 12:20.364
I don't… Pooping? No.

12:22.241 --> 12:23.367
Don't you need to go?

12:23.451 --> 12:25.202
Why are you asking me?

12:25.786 --> 12:27.246
Why are you getting annoyed?

12:27.830 --> 12:30.374
What do you want from us?
We can't go out, anyway.

12:32.334 --> 12:34.336
[breathes deeply]

12:34.920 --> 12:35.838
I have an idea.

12:40.801 --> 12:42.052
[Dae-su] First…

12:42.761 --> 12:44.430
The girls and the guys will take turns.

12:44.513 --> 12:45.848
Where?

12:46.724 --> 12:47.808
Here.

12:48.809 --> 12:50.269
[Hyo-ryeong] You're crazy.

12:50.352 --> 12:51.854
Stop it, man.

12:51.937 --> 12:52.938
[Dae-su] Why?

12:53.022 --> 12:57.109
The girls can wait in the other room,
and the guys can just pee out the window.

12:57.193 --> 12:59.320
What about… poop?

13:00.738 --> 13:01.780
Poop. Well…

13:02.490 --> 13:04.950
You can take off your pants
and hang out the window.

13:05.701 --> 13:06.535
Like this.

13:07.620 --> 13:08.496
Outside.

13:09.371 --> 13:11.540
Like you're taking a dump
at the edge of a cliff.

13:11.624 --> 13:13.626
-Like this.
-[Wu-jin] What reaction is he hoping for?

13:13.709 --> 13:15.836
-[Hyo-ryeong] Stop being ridiculous.
-[both sigh]

13:15.920 --> 13:18.422
But someone has to hold you,
so you don't fall.

13:18.506 --> 13:20.049
How are you going to wipe your butt?

13:20.925 --> 13:23.260
-Well, someone else should.
-[Hyo-ryeong] What is he saying?

13:23.344 --> 13:24.220
Idiot.

13:25.054 --> 13:26.472
Let's just hold it.

13:28.015 --> 13:29.266
If the rescuers come--

13:29.350 --> 13:31.143
It'll take a while for them to get here.

13:31.810 --> 13:35.606
It may be the same outside of the school.

13:36.815 --> 13:38.734
[On-jo] I don't know
how long we'll be stuck here,

13:38.817 --> 13:40.277
but my dad always told me

13:40.361 --> 13:42.655
to separate the bathroom
from where you sleep

13:42.738 --> 13:44.198
if you find yourself stranded.

13:44.782 --> 13:46.700
Where will we create a bathroom and how?

13:47.701 --> 13:48.994
Right there.

13:54.208 --> 13:55.709
-Yes, sir.
-[zombies gagging]

13:56.377 --> 13:58.087
-They're sending a chopper.
-[sighs]

13:58.170 --> 14:00.548
We have to get to the roof
by 11:00 a.m. tomorrow.

14:02.341 --> 14:04.134
What do you mean,
we have to go out to the roof

14:04.218 --> 14:05.678
when it's swarming with the infected?

14:05.761 --> 14:08.430
Also, 11:00 a.m. tomorrow?

14:08.514 --> 14:10.599
Why can't you arrange it
for 11:00 p.m. tonight?

14:10.683 --> 14:13.352
Yes, tomorrow. We'll spend the night here.

14:14.728 --> 14:17.982
How can the assemblywoman sleep here?
Radio in again!

14:18.065 --> 14:20.484
We'll have to stay here tonight,
so you're gonna have to create

14:20.568 --> 14:21.777
a temporary bathroom.

14:21.860 --> 14:23.320
-U-sin.
-Yes, sir.

14:27.408 --> 14:28.659
[sighs]

14:31.704 --> 14:35.416
Nam-ra and you guys, try to look
for something to cover the window.

14:35.499 --> 14:36.333
Okay.

14:36.417 --> 14:38.335
Cheong-san and Joon-yeong,

14:38.419 --> 14:42.089
make something that can absorb urine
and feces to use as a toilet.

14:44.383 --> 14:45.259
Cheong-san.

14:47.052 --> 14:48.846
And then the rest of you…

14:49.680 --> 14:50.514
A screen?

14:50.598 --> 14:52.182
-A screen?
-Yes, a screen to block.

14:57.021 --> 14:58.022
MUSIC 3

15:03.277 --> 15:04.778
Come with me. Come on.

15:04.862 --> 15:06.655
-That's the bathroom.
-[scoffs]

15:06.739 --> 15:07.573
[Dae-su groans]

15:21.211 --> 15:22.630
[Joon-yeong] Put this in here.

15:22.713 --> 15:25.966
Why don't we put this
on top of the basket?

15:26.050 --> 15:27.384
Oh, okay.

15:28.761 --> 15:31.555
Okay. We're all gonna
use this as a toilet,

15:31.639 --> 15:34.308
so that it will absorb urine and feces
as much as possible.

15:37.144 --> 15:38.562
[Cheong-san] Put this in there too.

15:39.647 --> 15:42.608
Dae-su's got a big butt, so let's…

15:43.901 --> 15:46.320
-[On-jo] Why don't we tape CDs up there?
-[tape screeching]

15:47.988 --> 15:49.573
-One more?
-Is there more tape?

15:49.657 --> 15:50.783
[tape screeching]

15:53.661 --> 15:56.497
-[clanking]
-[grunting]

15:59.750 --> 16:01.669
[boys grunt]

16:01.752 --> 16:04.505
What's going on?
Did they make the toilet yet?

16:04.588 --> 16:05.756
What's taking them so long?

16:09.802 --> 16:10.844
[Joon-yeong] That's good.

16:10.928 --> 16:13.222
-This should be good enough.
-[Joon-yeong] Okay.

16:14.264 --> 16:15.182
[grunts]

16:15.265 --> 16:16.600
[Dae-su] How do we poop on this?

16:16.684 --> 16:19.728
Use the cover for poop,
and without for pee.

16:19.812 --> 16:20.646
Get out.

16:20.729 --> 16:21.772
-Oh.
-Out.

16:21.855 --> 16:22.856
How do we use that?

16:22.940 --> 16:25.943
-Get out. Get out. Get out!
-Come on. Don't push me! Aah!

16:26.026 --> 16:27.194
-[unzips pants]
-[clangs]

16:27.861 --> 16:30.114
-[urine pattering]
-[sighs]

16:31.615 --> 16:32.491
[Joon-yeong grunting]

16:32.574 --> 16:34.994
At least there are cops
and soldiers out there, right?

16:37.037 --> 16:41.792
But if you watch the movies,
they can't do anything, either, right?

16:43.210 --> 16:45.337
Yeah, but they always save everyone
in the end.

16:48.048 --> 16:49.049
[sighs]

16:49.133 --> 16:50.884
-Here's the tissue.
-Pee. Just pee.

16:50.968 --> 16:52.803
-[both sniff]
-[door slams]

16:52.886 --> 16:54.555
-Oh!
-[Su-hyeok] Shit!

16:54.638 --> 16:56.557
-Why don't you just stay inside?
-[Ji-min groans]

16:56.640 --> 16:58.225
-[Dae-su] Does it smell?
-[door slams]

16:58.308 --> 16:59.935
-Shit.
-[Dae-su] What?

17:00.019 --> 17:03.063
Stop being so dramatic.
It doesn't smell at all.

17:03.147 --> 17:04.898
[Hyo-ryeong] Sit somewhere else.

17:05.566 --> 17:07.860
-[exhales deeply]
-There's nobody there.

17:07.943 --> 17:10.696
There are no lights on
in the stores and apartments out there.

17:11.363 --> 17:13.282
They all ran away or died.

17:13.365 --> 17:14.658
What do you mean by that?

17:14.742 --> 17:16.618
No one's coming here to save us.

17:18.245 --> 17:20.497
Why do you have to be so pessimistic?

17:20.581 --> 17:21.582
Don't you know my mom?

17:22.166 --> 17:25.586
She would've torn the school apart
looking for me, but she isn't here yet.

17:25.669 --> 17:26.795
So, what do you wanna do?

17:27.963 --> 17:30.090
I'm just trying to point out the facts.

17:30.174 --> 17:32.259
We all know that no one's coming.

17:32.926 --> 17:35.304
So I think we should just figure out
what we're gonna do next.

17:35.387 --> 17:37.181
We have to wait to be rescued.

17:37.806 --> 17:40.225
We can't leave somewhere safe
to go somewhere dangerous.

17:41.101 --> 17:42.728
And what if nobody comes?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.689
We haven't been waiting that long yet.

17:45.773 --> 17:47.816
How do you think we have to wait?

17:48.317 --> 17:51.278
-Do you think we should wait until we die?
-No.

17:51.361 --> 17:53.322
I'm saying let's wait as long as we can.

17:53.947 --> 17:55.824
There's no way we can go out
right now, anyway.

17:56.408 --> 17:58.118
[Su-hyeok] It's probably
because it's nighttime.

17:58.202 --> 18:00.579
I'm sure somebody will come
in the morning, maybe.

18:00.662 --> 18:02.706
There are a lot of choppers flying around.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.752
Let's just wait until tomorrow,
and we'll see.

18:12.883 --> 18:13.926
[gasps]

18:21.058 --> 18:23.477
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

18:24.770 --> 18:25.979
What do you mean?

18:26.063 --> 18:28.023
You're leaving first
for a personal matter?

18:29.191 --> 18:32.194
How could a firefighter say
something like this during a crisis?

18:32.277 --> 18:34.613
I'll take any punishment
when this is over.

18:34.696 --> 18:35.906
I'll resign if I have to.

18:36.782 --> 18:37.908
Listen.

18:37.991 --> 18:40.744
Do you intend to leave all these people
and go by yourself?

18:40.828 --> 18:44.498
You'll abandon your sick colleague
and leave a kid in charge?

18:45.207 --> 18:47.042
A kid? He's not a kid.

18:47.709 --> 18:48.752
He's a firefighter.

18:49.837 --> 18:50.921
[sighs]

18:56.844 --> 18:57.719
Fine.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.429
I made a mistake.

19:00.055 --> 19:02.766
Please accept my apologies.
I didn't mean to offend you.

19:03.851 --> 19:05.894
But this isn't just about you.

19:08.021 --> 19:09.189
My daughter is at school…

19:11.024 --> 19:12.025
but I can't reach her.

19:13.610 --> 19:15.028
I know she's waiting for me.

19:16.321 --> 19:17.239
[sighs]

19:18.240 --> 19:19.783
I need to go. I'm sorry.

19:19.867 --> 19:20.701
Stop. Wait.

19:20.784 --> 19:22.161
Let me tell you something.

19:28.417 --> 19:31.295
[Eun-hee] His apartment is right there.

19:32.880 --> 19:35.340
If he says he needs to go save his mother,

19:36.049 --> 19:37.217
do I let him go?

19:40.137 --> 19:42.014
And she lives right over there.

19:42.973 --> 19:45.184
She has a husband and children.

19:45.267 --> 19:47.895
Is it the right thing to do
to let her leave?

19:50.355 --> 19:52.399
Knowing they'll all die if they go out?

19:56.153 --> 19:57.696
I'll go even if I'll die.

19:58.739 --> 20:00.949
That's exactly why I'm saying this.

20:04.661 --> 20:06.246
You're a firefighter.

20:06.997 --> 20:08.498
I'm a politician.

20:10.500 --> 20:13.086
Do you know when it's the hardest
for people like us?

20:14.713 --> 20:15.881
Right now.

20:17.174 --> 20:19.176
Because we have to save the most people,

20:20.093 --> 20:22.554
not the people most precious to us.

20:26.558 --> 20:27.768
[exhales heavily]

20:35.067 --> 20:37.069
[leaves rustling]

20:42.407 --> 20:45.619
[zombies snarling]

20:46.828 --> 20:48.830
[suspenseful music]

20:51.708 --> 20:53.710
[whispering]
Fuck. Lucky me.

20:55.504 --> 20:57.130
All I gotta do is get to the bike.

20:57.214 --> 20:59.383
[leaves rustling]

20:59.466 --> 21:02.636
[growling]

21:02.719 --> 21:03.762
[panting]

21:03.845 --> 21:05.806
[growling]

21:10.978 --> 21:12.354
[clinks]

21:18.193 --> 21:20.862
[all growling]

21:26.576 --> 21:28.161
[chain rattles]

21:28.996 --> 21:30.122
Shit.

21:30.205 --> 21:32.541
[grunting]

21:32.624 --> 21:34.626
[all growling]

21:39.256 --> 21:41.466
[panting]

21:41.550 --> 21:43.093
[growling]

21:44.970 --> 21:46.972
[panting]

21:54.730 --> 21:56.398
[banging on door]

21:56.481 --> 21:58.191
[zombies growl]

21:58.275 --> 21:59.192
[grunts]

22:01.445 --> 22:02.738
[growls]

22:02.821 --> 22:03.655
[grunts]

22:06.491 --> 22:07.701
[bone crunches]

22:09.786 --> 22:11.121
[grunts]

22:12.956 --> 22:14.041
[growls]

22:15.208 --> 22:16.126
[grunts]

22:16.626 --> 22:18.628
[snarling]

22:28.597 --> 22:30.807
[all growling]

22:30.891 --> 22:34.352
[toilet flushes]

22:37.731 --> 22:39.775
Oh, damn! Wash up.

22:44.071 --> 22:45.989
Do you know where the juniors are?

22:46.656 --> 22:49.451
No, I don't know. Everyone's zombies.

22:49.534 --> 22:51.787
It's not like they'd stay
with their class.

22:51.870 --> 22:53.830
[lighter clicking]

22:53.914 --> 22:56.124
Stop that. You're driving me up the wall.

22:58.627 --> 23:00.170
It's dark now, right?

23:00.253 --> 23:01.213
[Mi-jin] Let's go.

23:02.839 --> 23:04.841
Let's just go tomorrow.
[sighs]

23:04.925 --> 23:08.428
It's too dark to see anything out there.
We won't see the zombies coming.

23:09.221 --> 23:12.099
Before you said we should go at night,
so the zombies don't see us.

23:12.766 --> 23:15.268
People change their minds
all the time, all right?

23:15.894 --> 23:17.312
Shut up and get up already!

23:17.938 --> 23:19.356
No, I'm not going.

23:19.439 --> 23:20.482
I swear to…

23:22.442 --> 23:23.610
Just forget it.

23:23.693 --> 23:25.946
Hey. Grab your arrows and follow me.

23:26.655 --> 23:28.156
Shut up and sit down.

23:29.074 --> 23:30.909
That fucker.

23:31.576 --> 23:33.537
Spoken like an athlete.

23:34.246 --> 23:37.374
-What?
-Doing nothing is your specialty.

23:37.457 --> 23:39.751
All you do is shoot arrows,
and you're gonna go to college

23:39.835 --> 23:41.711
and make a bunch of money.
You're life's easy,

23:41.795 --> 23:44.589
so all you know how to do
is sit on your ass and wait.

23:44.673 --> 23:46.800
Who says shooting arrows
gets you into college?

23:46.883 --> 23:47.926
Doesn't it?

23:48.009 --> 23:50.095
You're so fucking ignorant.
Be quiet already.

23:50.178 --> 23:51.263
You don't know anything.

23:51.346 --> 23:52.389
[Mi-jin] Fuck you.

23:53.181 --> 23:54.057
Hey.

23:54.891 --> 23:56.184
How'd you know?

23:56.268 --> 23:57.352
Hey.

23:58.770 --> 24:00.397
How'd you know I was ignorant?

24:01.148 --> 24:03.108
Huh? Is it on Facebook?

24:03.191 --> 24:05.610
Just stop. Let it go already.

24:05.694 --> 24:07.237
Why should she? She got hit.

24:07.863 --> 24:09.156
Hey, don't hold back.

24:09.906 --> 24:12.534
-[grunts]
-[clatters]

24:12.617 --> 24:13.910
-You fucking--
-[grunts]

24:16.079 --> 24:17.664
You little--
[grunts]

24:17.747 --> 24:19.082
Let go of me!

24:19.166 --> 24:20.834
[both grunting]

24:20.917 --> 24:22.627
-You shit, come at me!
-[Joon-seong] Stop it.

24:22.711 --> 24:23.712
-Come at me, bitch.
-[Min-jae] That's enough.

24:23.795 --> 24:24.671
Come down, stop.

24:24.754 --> 24:26.631
-[Joon-seong grunting]
-Come at me! Let go!

24:26.715 --> 24:27.632
Stop it!

24:27.716 --> 24:29.092
[Mi-jin] Get out of my way!

24:29.176 --> 24:30.177
[Joon-seong] Cut it out!

24:30.260 --> 24:31.845
-Hey.
-[Ha-ri] Let go of me.

24:31.928 --> 24:34.639
-Are you touching my boobs?
-[Min-jae grunting]

24:34.723 --> 24:35.807
Get lost.

24:35.891 --> 24:37.142
Come here! Come here!

24:37.225 --> 24:38.810
-Come on, just stop.
-[Mi-jin] Who do you think you are…

24:38.894 --> 24:39.853
[whispering]
People.

24:39.936 --> 24:41.396
ANYONE ALIVE?
ANYBODY THERE?

24:41.479 --> 24:43.982
This whole city is pure hell.

24:44.774 --> 24:46.359
The cops won't answer the phone.

24:46.443 --> 24:47.986
[breathing heavily]

24:48.069 --> 24:49.821
No first responders.

24:49.905 --> 24:50.989
Shit.

24:51.072 --> 24:53.366
LOOK AT HIS FACE LOL
YOU REALLY WENT?

24:53.450 --> 24:56.620
I'm going to hide
and wait for the rescuers.

24:57.370 --> 25:01.958
And please hit like
and subscribe to my channel, okay?

25:02.584 --> 25:05.795
Goddamnit. Can't you just like it
after I did all this?

25:05.879 --> 25:06.713
[woman screaming]

25:06.796 --> 25:09.049
IS THIS REAL?
I RESPECT YOU, BROTHER

25:09.132 --> 25:11.801
Okay. I'm going to go hide now.

25:12.594 --> 25:14.471
[breathing heavily]

25:14.554 --> 25:15.972
-[object clatters]
-Shit, shit, shit!

25:16.056 --> 25:19.100
Oh, my god. Who left their garbage here?

25:19.184 --> 25:21.895
MY CONDOLENCES
GARBAGE ASSHOLE LOL

25:21.978 --> 25:24.981
LET'S NOT GO THERE
ZOMBIES ARE LIVING CORPSES

25:25.065 --> 25:27.067
[crickets chirping]

25:33.073 --> 25:34.866
Look, everyone.

25:34.950 --> 25:36.243
I CAN'T TURN THIS OFF
COME BACK

25:36.326 --> 25:37.410
It's empty.

25:38.119 --> 25:39.371
I think it's safe.

25:39.454 --> 25:40.914
MY HEART'S RACING
I HATE ZOMBIES

25:40.997 --> 25:42.415
I'm going in now.

25:42.499 --> 25:45.669
THE SOUND MAKES IT SCARIER
IT'LL BE FULL OF ZOMBIES

25:45.752 --> 25:48.421
YOU'RE WORKING HARD
SHOULD'VE BROUGHT A GUN

25:48.964 --> 25:51.967
[door creaking]

25:52.050 --> 25:54.427
YOU SHOULD HIDE
STOP GOING

25:54.511 --> 25:57.430
BE CAREFUL
WHAT IF THEY'RE IN THERE?

25:57.514 --> 26:00.517
IT'S EMPTY, SPEND THE NIGHT
DON'T MAKE A SOUND!

26:00.600 --> 26:03.353
Okay, looks like no one's here.

26:03.436 --> 26:06.439
I'M SCARED…
SAFETY FIRST!

26:06.523 --> 26:10.443
IT'S TOO DARK…
IT'S NOT TOO LATE TO RUN…

26:10.527 --> 26:11.444
Hold on.

26:11.528 --> 26:12.612
[notification chimes]

26:12.696 --> 26:13.822
What is that?

26:13.905 --> 26:15.448
[snarling]

26:15.532 --> 26:18.535
[zombies screeching]

26:18.618 --> 26:20.245
[Orangibberish whimpers]

26:20.328 --> 26:21.454
Shit! Shit! Shit!

26:21.538 --> 26:23.415
Damn it.
[whimpers]

26:23.498 --> 26:24.916
RUN! RUN!
I WANT TO GO THERE TOO

26:25.000 --> 26:27.002
-[growling]
-[whimpering]

26:27.085 --> 26:28.169
[Orangibberish] This is bad.

26:31.423 --> 26:33.133
SO SCARY
IT'S ALL FAKE ANYWAY LOL

26:33.216 --> 26:34.926
IS THAT REAL?
KEEP STREAMING!

26:35.010 --> 26:36.094
Did you see all that?

26:36.177 --> 26:37.345
Where do I go now?

26:37.429 --> 26:39.431
[ominous music]

26:42.267 --> 26:43.727
[groans]

26:44.769 --> 26:47.772
-[grunting]
-[zombies growling]

26:47.856 --> 26:49.899
Oh, shit. Damn it.

26:50.734 --> 26:52.152
I'm surrounded.

26:52.235 --> 26:53.945
[all growling]

26:56.614 --> 26:58.742
[quivering]

26:59.701 --> 27:00.577
Do you have any idea

27:01.244 --> 27:03.496
what's going on out there?
You gotta tell me what you know.

27:07.751 --> 27:09.753
The strong are now ripping apart the weak.

27:10.962 --> 27:12.297
It happens all the time.

27:15.592 --> 27:16.593
Are you crazy?

27:16.676 --> 27:18.094
The world is crazy.

27:18.845 --> 27:20.096
Why did you do this?

27:21.181 --> 27:22.432
[scoffs]

27:22.515 --> 27:24.684
I tried to tell you,
but no one listened to me.

27:32.442 --> 27:33.443
[thuds on wall]

27:38.573 --> 27:41.659
My son was bullied for a very long time.

27:41.743 --> 27:45.163
[siren wailing]

27:50.752 --> 27:51.836
[bed clatters]

27:54.923 --> 27:57.926
[monitor beeping]

28:07.394 --> 28:09.729
[Byeong-chan] I only found out
when he tried to kill himself.

28:12.107 --> 28:13.483
It was too late.

28:14.651 --> 28:16.277
But I still thought I could fix it.

28:16.361 --> 28:18.488
SCHOOL VIOLENCE RESOLUTION COMMITTEE

28:18.571 --> 28:19.823
[Gwi-nam] We were just…

28:20.490 --> 28:21.866
You know…

28:23.535 --> 28:25.036
We were just fooling around.

28:30.417 --> 28:33.920
Come on, guys.
We were just messing around.

28:35.338 --> 28:37.549
That's what we do when we hang out, right?

28:40.176 --> 28:41.261
[mediator 1] Is that right?

28:48.226 --> 28:49.102
[mediator 2] Eun-ji?

28:50.895 --> 28:52.897
[somber music]

28:57.819 --> 28:58.695
Yes.

29:01.114 --> 29:02.282
[sighs]

29:03.742 --> 29:06.578
[indistinct chatter]

29:12.876 --> 29:14.627
[principal] They were just fooling around.

29:14.711 --> 29:16.755
Come on. Why would you go to the police?

29:16.838 --> 29:18.798
The school punished them. That's enough.
[chuckles]

29:18.882 --> 29:21.134
Writing a few apologies is punishment?

29:21.217 --> 29:22.719
They're just students.

29:22.802 --> 29:25.597
They apologized and promised
not to do it again. That's enough.

29:25.680 --> 29:27.265
We have the school evaluation coming up.

29:27.348 --> 29:30.185
Do you really wanna make an issue
out of it and blow it out of proportion?

29:30.268 --> 29:32.479
[Yong-nam] You're so right
about that, sir.

29:32.562 --> 29:35.190
You got yourself kicked out
of a pharmaceutical company

29:35.273 --> 29:36.858
and became a substitute teacher.

29:36.941 --> 29:40.028
Our principal took you in
as a permanent member of the faculty.

29:40.111 --> 29:41.571
You should be a team player

29:41.654 --> 29:43.573
and work for the school too.
[clicks tongue]

29:43.656 --> 29:45.283
[Byeong-chan] That's how they always were.

29:46.075 --> 29:47.243
[exhales heavily]

29:47.327 --> 29:49.662
We transferred him immediately
pretty much to run away.

29:50.872 --> 29:53.249
And they kept finding him
and harassing him.

29:54.709 --> 29:56.544
I guess it was fun for them.

29:57.754 --> 29:59.506
Like they're playing with a toy.

30:01.090 --> 30:03.843
[camera shutter clicking]

30:08.973 --> 30:11.935
[water dripping]

30:12.727 --> 30:14.020
Hey, Dad.

30:16.898 --> 30:17.899
[clatters]

30:18.900 --> 30:20.860
Just fight back, would you?

30:23.488 --> 30:26.282
Just be a man for once
and fight them back!

30:29.118 --> 30:30.703
I'm sorry, Dad.

30:31.871 --> 30:33.373
I just want to disappear.

30:36.751 --> 30:38.461
That would be easier for me.

30:40.046 --> 30:41.631
[Byeong-chan] That's when I realized it.

30:43.842 --> 30:46.010
We live in a system of assault.

30:47.428 --> 30:49.764
A complete nobody like me…

30:52.809 --> 30:54.352
can't change the system.

30:54.936 --> 30:56.145
[breathes shakily]

30:56.229 --> 30:58.231
[somber music continues]

31:06.656 --> 31:08.449
[Byeong-chan] So I decided
to change my son.

31:08.533 --> 31:10.577
[bubbling]

31:10.660 --> 31:12.745
I just hoped he wouldn't die.

31:13.705 --> 31:15.999
I didn't want him
to try and commit suicide again.

31:20.962 --> 31:22.338
[Jae-ik] You created…

31:26.467 --> 31:27.468
a monster.

31:28.761 --> 31:30.597
That's how desperate I was to save him.

31:32.265 --> 31:33.641
Rather than die as a human,

31:34.517 --> 31:36.561
I wanted him to survive as a monster.

31:38.396 --> 31:40.773
Don't you realize
that monster is killing everyone?

31:40.857 --> 31:43.443
Who cares if they all die?
They were all complicit.

31:43.526 --> 31:45.361
You crazy asshole.

31:46.112 --> 31:47.864
Who created this world?

31:47.947 --> 31:50.783
I warned that if you ignore it
for being a minor assault,

31:50.867 --> 31:53.036
violence would eventually rule the world.

31:53.119 --> 31:54.412
But no one listened to me.

31:55.121 --> 31:56.664
"It happens."

31:56.748 --> 31:58.041
"Kids fight."

31:58.124 --> 32:00.126
"They were bullied,
because they deserved it."

32:00.877 --> 32:03.254
The bastards who thought that
and shunned them

32:03.338 --> 32:05.632
made this world the hell
of what it is today!

32:09.218 --> 32:11.054
[breathes shakily]

32:18.686 --> 32:22.190
No. You're the one who made this hellhole.
It's on you.

32:22.815 --> 32:24.692
Maybe as a cop, I'm partly responsible.

32:25.318 --> 32:27.779
But what about those people out there
dying without knowing why?

32:27.862 --> 32:30.657
Sure. Maybe they're partly responsible
like you say.

32:30.740 --> 32:32.909
But there are certain things
you must pay with death,

32:32.992 --> 32:35.370
and certain things you must pay
as you live.

32:36.037 --> 32:39.332
You wanted to change the world.

32:41.376 --> 32:44.921
Not for everyone to die like this, huh.

32:51.094 --> 32:52.679
Day 39 of infection.

32:53.471 --> 32:55.515
I've tested several sedatives.

32:55.598 --> 32:56.975
The most effective…

32:59.060 --> 33:00.019
[breathes sharply]

33:02.772 --> 33:04.482
[growling]

33:06.567 --> 33:07.694
Where's the antidote?

33:09.320 --> 33:11.406
Well, there has to be
some kind of treatment.

33:13.866 --> 33:14.784
There's not.

33:23.668 --> 33:26.629
Let's go now. We have to evacuate.

33:28.631 --> 33:31.384
[sirens wailing]

33:42.562 --> 33:44.480
What are you looking at, asshole? Get on.

33:44.564 --> 33:45.857
Go ahead and shove them in.

33:46.607 --> 33:48.192
Yes, sir. Come on.

33:48.860 --> 33:51.362
Move quickly. Go. Go.

33:59.787 --> 34:04.542
[zombies snarling]

34:10.298 --> 34:14.135
-[gunshots]
-[people screaming]

34:22.977 --> 34:23.853
[gasping]

34:23.936 --> 34:26.064
Hey. What happened?

34:26.147 --> 34:27.982
-[distant shouting]
-[bone crunches]

34:28.983 --> 34:31.861
[growling]

34:34.405 --> 34:35.990
Holy shit.

34:36.074 --> 34:39.786
-[man groaning]
-[zombie snarling]

34:48.461 --> 34:50.463
[officer whimpering]

34:51.005 --> 34:52.548
[screaming]

34:54.759 --> 34:56.511
-[snarls]
-[screaming]

35:04.769 --> 35:09.065
[zombies growling]

35:09.148 --> 35:11.150
[foreboding music]

35:22.912 --> 35:25.832
[Byeong-chan] They're human beings
following their baseless instincts.

35:27.333 --> 35:29.585
That is just one side of human nature.

35:31.587 --> 35:33.798
Perhaps it's best to accept them
for what they are…

35:33.881 --> 35:34.966
[growling]

35:35.049 --> 35:37.802
…and simply give up
on trying to find a way to treat them.

35:37.885 --> 35:39.887
[foreboding music continues]

35:50.982 --> 35:56.195
[thwacking]

35:57.113 --> 35:58.573
[growls]

36:03.452 --> 36:05.872
[grunting]

36:05.955 --> 36:07.915
-[crunches]
-[yells]

36:09.750 --> 36:10.585
[groans]

36:14.672 --> 36:15.715
[grunts]

36:16.299 --> 36:17.884
My laptop is in the school science lab.

36:17.967 --> 36:18.801
Let's just go.

36:18.885 --> 36:21.554
If you try to find a solution to all this
in there, that's the only way.

36:21.637 --> 36:24.515
So let's get your laptop.
Come on. Let's go. Damn it.

36:27.518 --> 36:28.561
Byeong-chan!

36:28.644 --> 36:32.773
[shouting]
Go! Get out of here!

36:33.649 --> 36:35.276
[Byeong-chan] Go! Go now!

36:35.359 --> 36:38.070
[yelling]

36:44.535 --> 36:47.163
[banging on door]

36:48.206 --> 36:50.416
[growling]

36:54.837 --> 36:56.214
[snarls]

37:05.556 --> 37:09.560
[exhales deeply]
That was fucking close. What the fuck?

37:10.728 --> 37:14.148
[car zooming]

37:14.232 --> 37:15.233
[car crashes]

37:16.776 --> 37:21.155
-[whimpering]
-[growling]

37:24.283 --> 37:26.285
[suspenseful music]

37:31.374 --> 37:32.291
What the hell?

37:32.792 --> 37:35.253
-Wait. Wait, wait, wait. Wait. Wait.
-[man screaming]

37:35.336 --> 37:36.587
I'm stuck.

37:36.671 --> 37:37.964
I'm not a zombie.

37:39.548 --> 37:40.675
Here.

37:41.717 --> 37:44.929
[all snarling]

37:47.932 --> 37:50.559
[low growling]

37:56.732 --> 37:58.734
[ominous music]

38:00.403 --> 38:03.781
[Byeong-chan] The standards of being
humane emasculate human nature.

38:04.824 --> 38:06.575
How are we different from a seeing eye dog

38:06.659 --> 38:08.786
stripped of its basic instincts
to run and bark?

38:09.996 --> 38:13.249
Must all dogs forfeit their instincts
and become seeing eye dogs?

38:13.833 --> 38:16.836
Must all human beings abandon
their instincts to become humane?

38:28.014 --> 38:31.309
[growling]

38:33.394 --> 38:35.438
[screaming in distance]

38:35.521 --> 38:37.648
-[rapid footsteps]
-[growling]

38:40.109 --> 38:41.485
-Hey.
-Sir.

38:42.528 --> 38:44.280
We'll go to the
Emergency Management Agency

38:44.363 --> 38:47.783
to tell them to get the laptop
from the Hyosan High science lab.

38:47.867 --> 38:50.661
The solution to this disaster is in there.

38:50.745 --> 38:51.787
Got it?

38:51.871 --> 38:53.831
Hyosan High School.
Science lab. The laptop.

38:54.707 --> 38:55.666
Why are you telling me?

38:55.750 --> 38:59.003
If I die, you have to stay alive
and tell them. You understand, asshole?

38:59.086 --> 38:59.962
I do?

39:00.046 --> 39:01.505
Yes, you dumbass.

39:01.589 --> 39:02.798
Let's go.

39:02.882 --> 39:04.050
Whoa.

39:04.759 --> 39:05.718
Where are you going?

39:05.801 --> 39:08.095
The Emergency Management Agency.
I told you two seconds ago.

39:08.179 --> 39:10.264
Get your fucking head in the game.
Come on!

39:10.973 --> 39:12.933
-We're going where?
-Emergency Management.

39:13.017 --> 39:16.062
-And tell them what?
-Hyosan High, science lab, laptop.

39:16.145 --> 39:17.355
-That's right.
-Okay.

39:17.438 --> 39:19.482
-Are you ready?
-I'm not.

39:20.441 --> 39:21.359
Let's go.

39:21.442 --> 39:23.069
[breathes shakily]

39:27.656 --> 39:28.699
[grunts]

39:30.242 --> 39:31.243
Go with me.

39:31.327 --> 39:34.747
[distant screaming, whimpering]

39:44.924 --> 39:47.093
[snoring]

39:51.972 --> 39:54.600
[grunting]

39:55.601 --> 39:56.977
[sighs]
It's cold.

40:00.064 --> 40:02.066
[birds chirping]

40:22.920 --> 40:25.214
[snoring continues]

40:25.297 --> 40:27.299
[mellow music]

40:36.100 --> 40:37.560
[Cheong-san] No one came.

40:37.643 --> 40:40.271
[helicopters whirring in distance]

40:51.824 --> 40:53.576
[sighs]
This is insane.

40:54.285 --> 40:57.371
There are no cops. I have no cigarettes.

40:58.247 --> 40:59.498
[Mi-jin] There's no one here.

40:59.582 --> 41:02.835
Really? There's nobody? No one out there?

41:02.918 --> 41:03.919
Put me down.

41:04.003 --> 41:05.588
-[Mi-jin sighs]
-[Joon-seong groans]

41:05.671 --> 41:06.881
[Joon-seong] My back.

41:06.964 --> 41:08.215
[Mi-jin] Hey. Shit.

41:09.467 --> 41:11.010
[both exhale]

41:12.052 --> 41:13.762
Hey. What's the move?

41:14.513 --> 41:17.725
We have to leave.
No one's coming to save us.

41:20.561 --> 41:22.646
All the zombies will see us.

41:23.564 --> 41:24.899
Let's go at night.

41:24.982 --> 41:26.984
Okay. You can stay right here.

41:28.486 --> 41:30.988
Let's go out back, so we can try
and leave through the back gate.

41:31.071 --> 41:32.448
[Mi-jin] That's the fastest route.

41:32.531 --> 41:34.658
-I'm going to the second floor first.
-Why there?

41:35.451 --> 41:38.579
My brother's a junior.
I'll get him if he's in the classroom.

41:39.622 --> 41:43.792
Hey. Would a zombie really sit
and wait at his desk in his classroom?

41:45.461 --> 41:46.879
Did you see him turn into a zombie?

41:46.962 --> 41:48.464
He may have already.

41:48.547 --> 41:50.216
There's no guarantee he didn't.

41:50.758 --> 41:51.675
Shut up.

41:51.759 --> 41:53.511
Why are you arguing?

41:53.594 --> 41:54.887
Just fight, okay?

41:57.181 --> 41:58.057
Sorry.

42:01.977 --> 42:03.395
Come with me if you want.

42:09.235 --> 42:11.362
She's so cool. Fuck.

42:12.363 --> 42:13.364
So annoying.

42:16.825 --> 42:18.452
[sighs]
Wait up.

42:19.203 --> 42:20.955
They'll come for us eventually.

42:21.038 --> 42:22.498
How long do we wait?

42:23.332 --> 42:24.291
Until they come.

42:25.042 --> 42:26.835
There's no guarantee they'll come, though.

42:27.628 --> 42:29.880
So? You want to go out there?

42:29.964 --> 42:32.883
Even if they come, they won't find us
if they don't know we're here.

42:32.967 --> 42:35.302
Well, we can put up a sign for help.

42:35.386 --> 42:36.262
[Ji-min] How?

42:36.345 --> 42:40.182
I remember my dad taught me
a signal that's used internationally.

42:40.683 --> 42:41.892
[Hyo-ryeong] What is it?

42:42.893 --> 42:44.979
[On-jo] It's Cheong-san. Bye, Dad.

42:45.062 --> 42:46.772
[So-ju] Hey, have another bite. Okay?

42:46.855 --> 42:48.524
[So-ju] Hey, kid!

42:48.607 --> 42:52.194
It was red and blue arranged together

42:53.028 --> 42:57.950
to create some sort of a pattern.

43:05.082 --> 43:07.293
Should we write "SOS" on a curtain, maybe?

43:07.876 --> 43:09.044
Yeah, let's do that.

43:12.923 --> 43:14.550
[Nam-ra] We can't last long, anyway.

43:14.633 --> 43:15.926
Three minutes without oxygen,

43:16.010 --> 43:17.970
three days without water,
three weeks without food.

43:18.053 --> 43:19.221
What's that?

43:19.805 --> 43:21.223
How long a person can survive.

43:21.307 --> 43:24.727
It's only been a day, you know.
We have to try the best we can.

43:26.979 --> 43:28.731
We'll show signs of dehydration today.

43:28.814 --> 43:30.399
And we won't be able to move by tomorrow.

43:30.482 --> 43:32.192
What are you trying to say?

43:33.235 --> 43:34.695
Are you saying we should go out, or…

43:36.238 --> 43:40.075
are you saying we'll die, anyway,
so we shouldn't bother doing anything?

43:46.999 --> 43:47.958
I don't know.

43:48.042 --> 43:49.752
Then don't say anything.

43:52.254 --> 43:56.884
I think the prez means we should think
about anything else that we can do.

43:58.177 --> 43:59.011
[Su-hyeok] Right?

43:59.928 --> 44:01.221
-No.
-No?

44:02.598 --> 44:04.058
We don't know anything at all.

44:04.850 --> 44:06.894
We need to know something
before we can make plans.

44:06.977 --> 44:09.438
-[Ji-min] What more do we need to know?
-What Nam-ra means--

44:09.521 --> 44:12.399
You don't know what she's saying, either.

44:13.442 --> 44:14.318
No.

44:16.820 --> 44:19.865
Are you saying we need to understand
the situation in order to take action?

44:19.948 --> 44:22.660
Yes, that's right.

44:22.743 --> 44:24.244
Well, I totally agree with that.

44:25.162 --> 44:28.290
We need more information to decide
whether to wait, run, or get out.

44:28.374 --> 44:31.418
What can we find out on this situation,
and also, how?

44:31.502 --> 44:33.754
We can check online
if we have a cell phone.

44:35.255 --> 44:36.590
But we don't.

44:37.383 --> 44:38.509
The teacher's office.

44:41.720 --> 44:43.639
Why are you telling me that now?

44:43.722 --> 44:44.598
Sorry.

44:45.307 --> 44:48.394
Why are you telling me that, Cheol-su?
What do you want me to do about it?

44:48.477 --> 44:50.187
[sobbing]

44:52.773 --> 44:53.857
What time is it now?

44:53.941 --> 44:55.943
[ominous music]

44:56.610 --> 44:58.737
[Cheol-su] It's 9:00 a.m.

44:58.821 --> 45:02.157
-Hyosan High. Eun-ji.
-[keypad clacking]

45:02.825 --> 45:04.827
Nude. Kim Cheol-su.

45:04.910 --> 45:05.869
SCHEDULE SETTINGS

45:05.953 --> 45:07.913
[Gwi-nam] Schedule post…

45:07.996 --> 45:09.123
PROCESSING

45:09.206 --> 45:10.666
…for 9:00 a.m. tomorrow.

45:11.792 --> 45:13.001
Bring the money by nine.

45:13.877 --> 45:17.005
If you don't,
it'll be posted automatically.

45:21.009 --> 45:22.886
[Cheol-su] All I had to do
was give him money.

45:22.970 --> 45:26.056
But I couldn't because of the zombies.

45:26.140 --> 45:29.518
I was going to ask the rescuers
to find his phone if they came, but…

45:29.601 --> 45:31.061
It's past nine, right?

45:31.145 --> 45:32.729
Not sure. I don't have my phone.

45:33.397 --> 45:34.606
No way.

45:35.399 --> 45:36.567
It can't be nine yet.

45:37.067 --> 45:39.111
If that gets posted online, I'll…

45:40.028 --> 45:42.322
[quivering]

45:44.908 --> 45:47.536
What's wrong? Where are you going?
Where are you going?

45:47.619 --> 45:50.664
-Let go. I should've died yesterday.
-Don't do this.

45:51.290 --> 45:52.207
Please stop it!

45:52.291 --> 45:55.169
Whether or not you die,
the video will be posted.

45:55.711 --> 45:57.045
Nothing will change.

45:59.006 --> 46:02.176
[sobbing]

46:03.760 --> 46:05.137
I guess you're right.

46:05.762 --> 46:08.974
Even if I kill myself now,
everyone will still see my body.

46:09.892 --> 46:11.059
Everyone's gonna watch.

46:12.019 --> 46:12.978
And my mom…

46:13.562 --> 46:14.730
It'll be okay.

46:16.190 --> 46:17.983
We didn't do anything wrong.

46:18.066 --> 46:19.735
We were victims.

46:22.696 --> 46:23.614
I'm going.

46:24.573 --> 46:25.824
Where?

46:25.908 --> 46:27.534
-To get his phone.
-Are you insane?

46:30.037 --> 46:31.038
Come with me.

46:31.121 --> 46:33.707
-You filmed the whole thing.
-But…

46:33.790 --> 46:35.751
I had no choice. They made me do it.

46:35.834 --> 46:38.795
You pretty much committed murder
because you had no choice?

46:40.839 --> 46:41.757
Still…

46:43.425 --> 46:45.594
We'll die if we go.

46:45.677 --> 46:46.887
That's so you.

46:46.970 --> 46:49.598
You have no courage to live or die.

46:50.265 --> 46:52.226
You're such a fucking coward, Cheol-su.

47:09.701 --> 47:10.869
[door shuts]

47:11.912 --> 47:13.038
[lock clicks]

47:19.586 --> 47:20.462
Cheong-san.

47:21.672 --> 47:23.674
[On-jo] Stop being so stubborn.

47:25.384 --> 47:28.262
Two rooms across and one floor down
at the teacher's office.

47:28.345 --> 47:29.471
You shouldn't go.

47:29.555 --> 47:31.848
If I can't make it,
I'll just come back, you know?

47:32.683 --> 47:35.018
-Don't worry about me.
-I'm not worried about you.

47:35.519 --> 47:37.938
-I'm pissed off.
-Sure.

47:38.730 --> 47:40.607
Yes. Why would you worry about me?

47:45.028 --> 47:46.029
Shit.

47:49.324 --> 47:50.659
Su-hyeok.

47:50.742 --> 47:51.743
I'll be back soon.

47:51.827 --> 47:53.829
[suspenseful music]

47:57.374 --> 47:58.584
[Su-hyeok] Careful, Cheong-san.

48:01.253 --> 48:03.088
[Dae-su] Bare-su has always been
loyal to me.

48:03.171 --> 48:04.715
-[Wu-jin] You too?
-So I'm going too.

48:04.798 --> 48:07.384
-Stop. Come on. Get down.
-Why?

48:07.467 --> 48:09.511
You can't go out there
at your size, fatso.

48:10.220 --> 48:13.098
-My size?
-Are you serious?

48:17.019 --> 48:19.855
[grunting]

48:24.943 --> 48:26.278
Why do you keep following me?

48:27.362 --> 48:28.572
Who else do you have?

48:28.655 --> 48:29.656
[chuckles]

48:30.198 --> 48:31.366
You better stay close.

48:35.996 --> 48:36.997
Careful.

48:48.258 --> 48:49.635
Can we go in?

48:50.719 --> 48:51.553
Come back.

48:53.221 --> 48:55.140
[zombies snarling]

49:03.523 --> 49:04.775
What are you gonna do?

49:08.695 --> 49:10.280
Let's hang by our hands and go across.

49:12.699 --> 49:14.534
No, I don't mean that.

49:15.827 --> 49:18.288
I heard On-jo told you that she likes you.

49:19.456 --> 49:22.334
-Are you going to go out with her?
-Is that important right now?

49:24.503 --> 49:27.673
I'm not asking because it's important.
I'm just curious. That's all.

49:29.675 --> 49:30.509
Why?

49:31.760 --> 49:33.345
-Do you think I should?
-Hey.

49:34.096 --> 49:35.514
Why would you even ask me that?

49:36.139 --> 49:37.766
Do whatever you want. Who cares?

49:37.849 --> 49:39.351
What do you think?

49:40.894 --> 49:41.895
Go.

49:46.483 --> 49:47.317
Go.

49:47.401 --> 49:48.276
You go.

49:52.280 --> 49:53.115
Be careful.

49:53.198 --> 49:55.200
[tense music]

49:56.576 --> 49:59.996
[both grunting]

50:07.504 --> 50:09.423
[snarling]

50:10.757 --> 50:13.844
[growling]

50:16.680 --> 50:20.183
[Eun-ji screaming]

50:29.943 --> 50:31.778
[growling]

50:40.287 --> 50:42.789
Why are you doing this to me?

50:43.623 --> 50:45.876
[wailing]

50:45.959 --> 50:47.377
Wait, wait, wait. Shh.

50:47.461 --> 50:49.796
[Eun-ji wailing]

50:49.880 --> 50:52.966
[flesh squelching]

51:00.932 --> 51:04.102
[snarling]

51:15.655 --> 51:17.866
[growling]

51:29.628 --> 51:33.840
[growling]

51:41.139 --> 51:44.100
[tense music continues]

51:46.478 --> 51:47.729
[snarling]

51:56.279 --> 51:58.240
[snarling]

51:59.324 --> 52:00.283
[door slides]

52:00.367 --> 52:01.535
[thuds]

52:02.452 --> 52:05.455
[all growling]

52:20.011 --> 52:22.597
[thumping]

52:24.474 --> 52:25.642
What is that sound?

52:26.601 --> 52:28.937
I don't know. Let's go see.

52:29.020 --> 52:30.856
[Eun-ji groaning]

52:42.117 --> 52:45.036
Fucking die!

52:45.120 --> 52:49.082
[cell phones crashing]

52:50.625 --> 52:51.960
What is it?

52:52.836 --> 52:54.212
[grunting]

52:54.838 --> 52:56.089
[bone crunches]

52:56.172 --> 52:57.507
[groans]

53:03.346 --> 53:05.432
[groaning continues]

53:05.515 --> 53:06.683
[bone crunches]

53:08.476 --> 53:10.478
[grunting]

53:11.897 --> 53:12.731
[chimes]

53:12.814 --> 53:13.899
GWI-NAM
UPLOAD

53:15.609 --> 53:18.945
-[grunting]
-[thumping]

53:24.659 --> 53:26.536
[grunting continues]

53:30.540 --> 53:33.376
-[Eun-ji grunting]
-[thumping]

53:40.050 --> 53:42.093
[grunting continues]

54:01.446 --> 54:03.406
I'm gonna kill you!

54:05.575 --> 54:07.744
Give it to me, fucker! I'll kill you!

54:12.874 --> 54:13.875
Cheong-san.

54:13.959 --> 54:15.627
[all growling]

54:18.755 --> 54:19.923
[grumbles]

54:21.633 --> 54:23.551
[growling]

54:26.221 --> 54:27.305
[grunts]

54:36.439 --> 54:37.732
[Cheong-san] You go! I'll meet you there!

54:39.109 --> 54:40.652
Damn it.
[yells]

54:43.196 --> 54:44.614
-[snarls]
-[grunts]

54:50.954 --> 54:53.832
[growling]

54:56.710 --> 54:57.877
Hey.

54:57.961 --> 54:59.713
-Hey, wake up.
-[whimpers]

55:01.798 --> 55:03.091
You're Gwi-nam, right?

55:03.174 --> 55:04.509
What? Why?

55:05.218 --> 55:07.220
How is it outside? Still the same?

55:09.723 --> 55:10.807
[groans]

55:11.599 --> 55:12.934
I don't know.

55:14.561 --> 55:16.229
You can drive the car, right?

55:16.855 --> 55:19.024
-I can't.
-Come on!

55:19.107 --> 55:21.860
I had cover up your mess last year
when you guys drove your dad's car

55:21.943 --> 55:23.361
and cause an accident!

55:24.279 --> 55:25.572
Why do you ask?

55:28.992 --> 55:30.618
Here's my car key.
It's in the parking lot.

55:30.702 --> 55:32.287
License plate, 7340.

55:34.539 --> 55:36.458
Bring it here.

55:41.546 --> 55:42.505
Why?

55:43.089 --> 55:45.717
Go to the night duty room
and out the window, it's in the lot.

55:46.634 --> 55:48.511
No way.
[groans]

55:49.137 --> 55:51.389
You punk.
Listen to your principal at once!

55:51.473 --> 55:52.891
I said no.

55:56.853 --> 55:58.354
-Give me that. Give me that.
-You punk.

55:58.438 --> 56:00.648
-[grunts]
-I said to let go.

56:01.316 --> 56:02.400
Damn it.

56:04.778 --> 56:06.196
Fine. Just get out of here.

56:06.279 --> 56:07.113
Go with me.

56:07.197 --> 56:09.074
Why should I? You go.

56:09.157 --> 56:10.867
[Gwi-nam] Go with me to the car.

56:10.950 --> 56:14.788
It'd be nice to have a shield, anyway.

56:14.871 --> 56:16.790
What's wrong with you? Stay away.

56:16.873 --> 56:17.874
-[grunts]
-[clanks]

56:18.750 --> 56:20.502
My god. Look at you.

56:22.420 --> 56:25.048
All right, Mr. Principal.

56:25.131 --> 56:26.508
If this were a game,

56:27.008 --> 56:27.967
I'd be…

56:29.469 --> 56:30.762
happy to kill you…

56:31.930 --> 56:32.972
sir.

56:33.056 --> 56:35.058
[ominous music]

56:38.895 --> 56:41.898
[snarling]

56:44.567 --> 56:45.652
[squelches]

56:58.248 --> 56:59.124
Are you okay?

56:59.207 --> 57:00.208
Yes.

57:01.501 --> 57:04.587
All right. Let's go.
We need to go to the roof now.

57:05.380 --> 57:07.674
Please, everyone, work together
like we practiced.

57:07.757 --> 57:10.969
-[growling]
-[grunting]

57:11.052 --> 57:12.387
Hurry!

57:12.971 --> 57:14.264
What's taking so long?

57:15.098 --> 57:16.099
Hold on!

57:17.392 --> 57:18.852
I'll do it. Block them.

57:18.935 --> 57:20.270
-With the desk. Hurry!
-Yes, sir!

57:20.353 --> 57:22.147
-Come with me.
-Okay! Okay!

57:28.278 --> 57:30.155
Okay, come one by one. One by one.

57:31.156 --> 57:33.074
Madam, please go.

57:33.158 --> 57:34.784
-You go first.
-No, you go first!

57:34.868 --> 57:37.287
-Just anyone! Come on!
-Go! Hurry!

57:39.122 --> 57:40.874
Go! Hurry! Go!

57:40.957 --> 57:42.834
[growling]

57:45.003 --> 57:46.754
Okay. Run on my signal.

57:48.506 --> 57:50.967
Three! Two! One!

57:51.676 --> 57:54.512
-Now!
-[men yelling]

57:55.847 --> 57:56.723
Get back!

58:07.150 --> 58:08.651
Get back!

58:08.735 --> 58:10.278
[So-ju grunting]

58:13.364 --> 58:14.741
Hurry! Hurry!

58:17.619 --> 58:19.204
-Back up!
-Yes, sir!

58:25.752 --> 58:26.753
I've got it!

58:32.425 --> 58:33.551
What now?

58:33.635 --> 58:34.594
Hello?

58:38.264 --> 58:39.641
Close the door!

58:41.351 --> 58:42.519
-[grunts]
-[zombies snarling]

58:42.602 --> 58:44.103
Captain, below, below!

58:47.190 --> 58:49.734
[water splashing]

58:57.200 --> 58:58.868
Captain, in here too!

58:59.619 --> 59:00.828
[door banging]

59:02.121 --> 59:04.457
[growling]

59:11.214 --> 59:12.173
Come upstairs now!

59:12.257 --> 59:13.550
Go up first.

59:13.633 --> 59:14.467
We can't.

59:15.468 --> 59:17.303
The door to the roof is locked.

59:17.387 --> 59:18.388
What?

59:18.471 --> 59:20.098
The door is locked!

59:21.307 --> 59:23.726
-U-sin, do you have the tools?
-Yes, I do.

59:24.477 --> 59:26.187
-Go upstairs.
-What about the door?

59:26.271 --> 59:27.438
Come on!

59:29.566 --> 59:30.650
Go up now! Come on!

59:31.651 --> 59:32.569
[Dal-ho] Hurry!

59:34.946 --> 59:36.072
[door banging]

59:36.155 --> 59:38.157
[growling]

59:43.997 --> 59:45.081
[grunting]

59:50.003 --> 59:52.088
-Get out of the way. Get out of the way.
-Step aside.

01:00:02.515 --> 01:00:03.975
[grunts]

01:00:04.058 --> 01:00:05.602
Help him! Come on.

01:00:05.685 --> 01:00:10.356
[all grunting]

01:00:15.737 --> 01:00:19.157
-Okay. One, two…
-[all grunt]

01:00:19.240 --> 01:00:21.117
[all growling]

01:00:23.119 --> 01:00:26.164
[growling]

01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:31.502
[tense music]

01:00:37.091 --> 01:00:38.968
[grunting]

01:00:39.802 --> 01:00:41.304
[snarling]

01:00:46.601 --> 01:00:49.062
-[grunting continues]
-[lock clangs]

01:00:50.271 --> 01:00:52.315
[growling]

01:00:52.398 --> 01:00:53.900
[So-ju grunting]

01:00:56.903 --> 01:00:58.780
-Hurry, ma'am.
-After you, ma'am.

01:00:58.863 --> 01:01:00.657
Careful. Go. Go.

01:01:00.740 --> 01:01:02.742
[men panting]

01:01:02.825 --> 01:01:05.578
[So-ju groaning]

01:01:16.756 --> 01:01:19.133
[So-ju groaning]

01:01:22.887 --> 01:01:27.308
[breathing deeply]

01:01:42.115 --> 01:01:43.324
Holy shit, sir.

01:01:43.408 --> 01:01:45.493
Hurry up, sir! Hurry!

01:01:49.038 --> 01:01:50.081
What happened?

01:01:51.416 --> 01:01:53.668
Careful. Hold on. Hurry, hurry.

01:01:55.878 --> 01:01:56.754
[slams]

01:01:58.965 --> 01:02:01.342
[breathes heavily]

01:02:17.692 --> 01:02:19.360
You all did great in there.

01:02:20.653 --> 01:02:22.155
Is anybody injured?

01:02:22.238 --> 01:02:24.741
[helicopter whirring]

01:02:27.952 --> 01:02:30.955
[hissing]

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:46.262
[growling]

01:02:53.770 --> 01:02:55.772
[thrilling music]

01:03:06.657 --> 01:03:09.494
[banging on door]

01:03:11.746 --> 01:03:13.790
-Is that the principal?
-Get this jerk off my back!

01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:15.249
-Get this psychopath!
-Shh!

01:03:15.333 --> 01:03:16.459
What the hell, Gwi-nam?

01:03:16.542 --> 01:03:17.543
[Gwi-nam] Cheong-san.

01:03:17.627 --> 01:03:19.295
Come here and tie his arms.

01:03:19.796 --> 01:03:21.339
The bastard won't stay still.

01:03:21.923 --> 01:03:23.674
Hey. What are you doing?

01:03:24.967 --> 01:03:26.427
Come and tie him up.

01:03:26.511 --> 01:03:29.138
You're finished. Do you hear me?
I'm expelling you! Untie me now!

01:03:29.222 --> 01:03:30.932
[whimpers]

01:03:31.015 --> 01:03:31.974
Gwi-nam!

01:03:32.058 --> 01:03:33.267
Stop that.

01:03:35.520 --> 01:03:38.606
Stop what? This fucking guy…

01:03:40.233 --> 01:03:41.400
tried to kill me.

01:03:44.779 --> 01:03:47.532
-He said to go out and get his car!
-[whimpering]

01:03:48.115 --> 01:03:49.617
You call yourself a principal.

01:03:50.451 --> 01:03:52.203
-Hey.
-That's right. Good idea.

01:03:52.829 --> 01:03:53.996
I'm filming everything.

01:03:54.789 --> 01:03:57.124
Let go, or I'm gonna send this
to the police immediately.

01:03:57.208 --> 01:03:59.794
You little… I will kill you.

01:03:59.877 --> 01:04:02.046
Just stop acting like human garbage.

01:04:03.422 --> 01:04:05.383
No one respects you
just because you act tough.

01:04:05.466 --> 01:04:07.218
I'm the new boss of this school.

01:04:08.427 --> 01:04:10.555
-Don't you get it?
-Don't make me laugh.

01:04:11.556 --> 01:04:15.393
You're just a fucking loser
who will serve bullies…

01:04:16.310 --> 01:04:17.562
for his entire life.

01:04:18.563 --> 01:04:19.689
[knife clinks]

01:04:24.986 --> 01:04:26.863
Yeah? Say that again.

01:04:27.738 --> 01:04:28.656
Huh?

01:04:30.533 --> 01:04:32.535
[yells, chokes]

01:04:38.040 --> 01:04:39.375
You fucking…

01:04:40.376 --> 01:04:41.836
[clinking]

01:04:43.170 --> 01:04:45.256
So am I…

01:04:45.965 --> 01:04:47.383
still a loser?

01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:51.178
Are you with me or not? The phone.

01:04:51.762 --> 01:04:53.514
-You just murdered--
-Give me the phone!

01:04:53.598 --> 01:04:55.224
[both grunting]

01:04:57.143 --> 01:04:58.978
[groaning]

01:05:00.605 --> 01:05:01.522
[both grunting]

01:05:06.986 --> 01:05:07.862
Damn it!

01:05:07.945 --> 01:05:10.156
[panting]

01:05:12.867 --> 01:05:14.201
[growling]

01:05:16.037 --> 01:05:17.788
[panting]

01:05:17.872 --> 01:05:20.666
[tense music]

01:05:22.585 --> 01:05:23.669
[grunts]

01:05:39.310 --> 01:05:41.312
[closing theme music]

01:09:18.863 --> 01:09:22.950
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS SHOW ARE FICTIONAL.
